# Block 1: lidar_gmrt_elevation
# DECLINE: Terrain DEM — the GMRT (Global Multi-Resolution Topography)
# PointServer returns seafloor depth at a queried lon/lat from a compiled
# multibeam-sonar synthesis grid, not a live measurement stream. Geographic
# infrastructure (terrain DEM) fails the Force Gate; the block also declares
# no frame, so the parser would refuse it.
# Old block: https://www.gmrt.org/services/PointServer?longitude={lon}&latitude={lat}&format=json | force em | ttl 86400

# Block 2: lidar_lola_moon_elevation
# DECLINE: Derived point-cloud product — the STAC query returns LOLA tile
# statistics (pc:statistics.2 mean/min/max), a compiled lunar DEM summary,
# not individual laser returns. Derived topography products fail the Force
# Gate; the 0 0 lat/lon is a query footprint on the moon, not a terrestrial
# frame.
# Old block: https://g6goyz4w56.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/prod/collections/lunar_orbiter_laser_altimeter/items?limit=1 | force em | ttl 86400

# Block 3: lidar_lola_moon_point_cloud
# DECLINE: Bare count — pc:count is the number of points in a tile and
# pc:density a derived per-area ratio; no individual laser events. Bare
# counts without individual events fail the Force Gate.
# Old block: https://g6goyz4w56.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/prod/collections/lunar_orbiter_laser_altimeter/items?limit=1 | force em | ttl 86400

# Block 4: lidar_mola_mars_megdr_count
# DECLINE: Bare count — regex <Count> extracts the tally of MOLA MEGDR
# products in a PDS archive. A catalog count with no individual measurements;
# no organism senses an archive tally.
# Old block: https://oderest.rsl.wustl.edu/live2/?query=PRODUCT&target=Mars&IHID=MGS&IID=MOLA&PT=MEGDR&output=XML | force em | ttl 86400

# Block 5: lidar_mola_mars_pedr_count
# DECLINE: Bare count — regex <Count> extracts the tally of MOLA PEDR
